# GitHub Personal Access Token (classic)
#
# Required for build-time GitHub stats on the /about page:
#  - Contribution calendar (heatmap)
#  - Pinned repositories
#  - Language breakdown
#  - Follower / following counts
#
# Without this token, the about page falls back to mock data.
#
# How to create one:
#   1. Go to https://github.com/settings/tokens
#   2. Click "Generate new token (classic)"
#   3. Give it a name (e.g. "ricki-web build")
#   4. No scopes needed — the GraphQL API returns public data without
#      any selected scopes.  (Selecting `read:user` or `repo` also works.)
#   5. Copy the generated token here.
#
GITHUB_TOKEN=
